"1435","Mario Krieger","Mario","Krieger","I studied mechanical engineering and have about 5 years of experience in the development of medical devices and injection molding tools. I am currently completing my physiotherapist training until September 2024.","https://linkedin.com/in/mario-krieger","The Hague, South Holland, Netherlands","Netherlands","The Hague, South Holland","38","38","When I started my master's studies, I started working in the development team for prosthetic feet at OTTOBOCK, where I also wrote my master's thesis on developing a prosthetic foot with low production costs for countries with poor healthcare.

After my master's thesis, I took a full-time position in development at Junghans Kunststoffwaren-Fabrik. There I developed packaging products for the food industry. It included the development of the product itself, the production process and everything around it, including 3D simulation and the design of the injection molding tools. In this job, I really learned a lot about processing, production and of course injection molding.

In October 2019, I moved to the city of Hamburg to join the WEINMANN development team. My tasks included the development of plastic housings for ventilation devices for ambulances. Later, I was additionally involved in some development processes, for example the development of a pressure relief valve or a test lung to check the ventilation devices.

