"2472","Jens Pawlik","Jens","Pawlik","Technology expert, mechanical design at Danfoss","https://linkedin.com/in/jens-pawlik-0b57208","Region of Southern Denmark, Denmark","Denmark","Region of Southern Denmark","297","292","","Software Development, Ansys Mechanical APDL, Manufacturing, Injection Molding, Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD), Simulation automation, CAD Parameterization, Polymer Material Calibration, New Hire Training, Consulting, MDO(Multidisciplinary Design Optimization), Design of Experiments (DOE), Structural simulation, Material Characterization, Cross-functional Collaborations, Mechanical Engineering, Structural Analysis, Mechanical Testing, CAD, Optimization, Root Cause Analysis, Reliability Engineering, Measurements, Refrigeration, Design for Manufacturing, HVAC, Additive Manufacturing, ANSYS, Finite Element Analysis (FEA)","","Danfoss Climate Solutions","Senior Specialist, Mechanical Design","In 2019 our Virtual Competence Center was formed, and I joined the VCC from day one. Over a few years we increased head-count from 3 to about 15 people, and I was a big part of the onboarding and strategy creation.
Developments to mention:
* Won an internal Danfoss competition ""Man on the Moon"" with creation of a MDO model. In short, the MDO starts with a parametric CAD of a valve that is used to simulate burst pressure of the valve (FEA), flow properties of the valve (CFD), estimate cost of the specific model (should-cost-analysis). The responses of each design is used to create a meta model, that is then used in an optimization loop. Cost of pilot product was reduced by more than 40%
*Creation of fully automized webapp-based workflow for burst simulations. Via python code a work flow is created and executed based on a 3D file uploaded by the user. The solver process runs in the back ground, and when finished, python is used to extract results from the simulation, compile them in a PDF report, that the user can download.","Jan 2019 - Present · 7 yrs 7 mos","Danfoss","Technology expert, mechanical design","Frontend development projects / technology explorations within the refrigeration segment:
The Tech Expl. are ""mini projects"" with an average of 3 months timeline, and are all about converting hypothesis and ideas coming from marketing, innovation group, sales, or other parts of the organization into prototypes and testing these in application setups. Projects are typically on component level or sub-system level of residential, commercial or industrial refrigeration applications.
 
Internal consultancy, Structural analysis:
Supporting R&D, engineering, production in various problems/challenges by means of FEA:
* Static structural (Burst simulations, Creep, Swaging and other plastic deformations, contact   problems, etc.)
* Implicit and explicit thermal simulations, often coupled to static
* Parameter variation/optimization
Gradually the consultancy role on mechanical simulations grew from around 30% to 100% dedicated simulation work
Software usage:
Minitab (Statistics, reliability and DoE)
Ansys mechanial (WB)
Autodesk Inventor (also used ProE and Unigraphics in former jobs)
modeFrontier (optimization software)
Mindjet (Root cause problem solving)
