"2607","Mia Katharina A Podlech","Mia Katharina A","Podlech","Polymer Specialist-Bring Out the Best in Polymers | Chemical Engineer| Polymer & Material testing| Compounder| Formulation specialist| Lab. Manager| Sustainability Management| GHG-protocol| Stakeholder Engagement| #ONO","https://linkedin.com/in/mia-katharina-a-podlech","Greater Esbjerg Area","Denmark","Greater Esbjerg Area","938","936","Profile
I turn deep polymer knowledge into robust, sustainable products by connecting material, process and performance. With a strong analytical mindset and a collaborative approach, I help organisations move from complexity to clarity - and from ideas to results.
 
 I am a polymer specialist with deep and thorough knowledge regarding polymer science and technology. To bring out the best in polymers, I consistently apply a systemic approach considering part design, manufacturing process and material. My experience spans polymers including thermoplastics, thermosets, thermoplastic elastomers, rubber & rubber formulation, adhesives and adhesive technology, as well as synthetic textiles. I work confidently across process technology such as injection moulding, 2K, casting and compression moulding.

 I am highly data-driven and self-directed, using material testing, characterisation and qualification (test set-ups and programmes, accelerated lifetime tests, service life prediction and Design of Experiments) to translate end-to-end product and component functionality into clear material requirements. I ”attack” problems with curiosity and persistence, always seeking the link between polymer structure, processing and final performance.
 
What I am most proud of: 
- Extending the lifetime of wind turbine blades through material selection of leading edge protection, contributing to more durable and sustainable renewable energy solutions.
- Development of a PFAS-free pump: Leading the replacement of a fluoropolymer to eliminate PFAS – a project completed with rigorous experimental work, deep polymer expertise, and culminating in a successful launch to key customers.
- Driving and establishing the first Greenhouse Gas Protocol, incl. identifying emission reduction opportunities and a more strategic sustainability approach.
    
My motivation comes from creating tangible environmental and societal value, particularly through sustainability and the responsible use of polymers in sustainable consumption and production patterns. I thrive on collaboration, knowledge sharing and working with skilled, trustworthy people - while keeping the atmosphere positive and human.

