"2624","Jesper Bogelund","Jesper","Bogelund","Sustainability Scientist at Novo Nordisk A/S","https://linkedin.com/in/jesperbogelund","Region Zealand, Denmark","Denmark","Region Zealand","898","881","MSc in Materials Chemistry, specialized in plastics and environmental analysis. Since 2018 engaged in the Circular for Zero strategy trying to find environmentally benign methods to deliver medical treatments to users.

I started my studies in Natural Science at the University of Southern Denmark (Odense Universitet) in 1992 out of an conviction in that we should use scientific knowledge and technological development to build a sustainable future while increasing the comfort of living. After the basic courses in math, physics, chemistry and biology, my studies went in the direction of ecotoxicology and environmental chemistry.
In the mid-90’s I transferred to Copenhagen and studied environmental chemistry and materials chemistry at the University of Copenhagen. My special interest was on surface chemistry and understanding how molecules interact with solid surfaces. I finished the studies in 1999 and have been working with polymer materials ever since, with special focus on the interdisciplinary approach to understanding ageing mechanisms, failure analysis and materials development. 
Since 2005 I have had a special interest in understanding nanocomposites; an ideal nanocompisite material should be dominated by interface effects e.g. the confinement effects on polymer chain dynamics. Since 2010 I re-gained my interest in the assessment of the environmental aspects of our use of materials through the use of life cycle analytical approaches.
