"2740","Peter Alexandersen","Peter","Alexandersen","Project manager","https://linkedin.com/in/peter-alexandersen","Ry, Central Denmark Region, Denmark","Denmark","Ry, Central Denmark Region","480","475","I have through the last 20 years, worked as technical project manager and project manager, with 17 years within the plast industry, with focus on product development, design, molding tools and plast production. In my 26 years as engineer, I have always had a cross functional role, working with different stakeholder, organizations, suppliers and customers within DK, but also in Europe and Asia.

I was almost 17 years at Danfoss A/S, centrally located in the develop department, with responsibility for DFM, purchasing/specifying of molding tools and implementation in our own molding factory, and ensuring the quality within the plast production. 

My daily work involves collaborating across organizations and countries to ensure the interests of my stakeholders and to ensure the best solution for the customer/company, in both development, production and problem solving. I have therefore had a wide range of partners from product owners, designers, plast makers, plast production, toolmakers, quality department, to various customers and subcontractors.
I have spent a lot of time in our plast production, together with plast makers in connection with new products, but also at the assembly line as needed. 

With my position as project manager, with external customers and internal development departments, respectively being proactive and front-loading has been an important task for risk management, planning, resources, and finances, in the projects, but also in the decision-making process for me or any management team.

